  <h1 id="GameFramework_Input_Handlers" data-uid="GameFramework.Input.Handlers" class="text-break">Namespace GameFramework.Input.Handlers
  </h1>
  <div class="markdown level0 summary"></div>
  <div class="markdown level0 conceptual"></div>
  <div class="markdown level0 remarks"></div>
    <h3 id="classes">Classes
  </h3>
      <h4><a class="xref" href="GameFramework.Input.Handlers.ConsoleInputHandler.html">ConsoleInputHandler</a></h4>
      <section><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.Input.Handlers.ConsoleInputHandler.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="3">Handles console input - always active, highest priority
When console is open, consumes most input to prevent conflicts</p>
</section>
      <h4><a class="xref" href="GameFramework.Input.Handlers.PlayerInputHandler.html">PlayerInputHandler</a></h4>
      <section><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.Input.Handlers.PlayerInputHandler.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="3">Handles player input - only active during gameplay
Lower priority than UI to ensure menus can override player actions</p>
</section>
      <h4><a class="xref" href="GameFramework.Input.Handlers.UIInputHandler.html">UIInputHandler</a></h4>
      <section><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.Input.Handlers.UIInputHandler.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="3">Handles UI input - active when any UI is visible
High priority to ensure UI interactions work correctly</p>
</section>
</article>
